.TH MEM 3
.SH NAME
mem \- memory buffer routines
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.ft CW
#include <ast.h>

void*   memdup(const void* \fIbuf\fP, size_t \fIn\fP)
void*   memzero(void* \fIbuf\fP, size_t \fIn\fP);
.ft
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f(CWmemdup\fP
copies the
.I n
byte buffer
.I buf
to a new location provided by
.IR malloc (3)
and returns a pointer to the new copy.
0 is returned if
.IR malloc (3)
fails.
.PP
\f(CWmemzero\fP
sets the first
.I n
bytes in
.I buf
to
.IR 0 .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.br
.IR str (3),
.IR malloc (3)
